================================================================================
CAMERA DATABASE
================================================================================

Crate includes a camera database feature (Settings → Camera Database)
that allows users to maintain a personal database of camera sensor
specifications for use with Nuke's Camera nodes.

The Camera module ships with a reference database of digital cinema,
broadcast, drone, mobile, and film camera sensor specifications. This
data is derived in part from VFXCamDB (https://vfxcamdb.com/) and Matchmove Machine
(https://camdb.matchmovemachine.com/), both of whom have granted
permission for their databases to be used in Crate.

The Camera module would not exist in its
current form without the work of VFXCamDB and Matchmove Machine.
If you find this data useful, please consider supporting VFXCamDB
(https://vfxcamdb.com/donate/) and Matchmove Machine
(https://camdb.matchmovemachine.com/donate) directly.

Any inaccuracies in Crate's database are ours, not VFXCamDB's or
Matchmove Machine's. Corrections are welcome via the issue tracker at
https://github.com/CrateTools/CrateCamDB, and significant corrections
will be reported back to the parent databases.

Users may extend, edit, or replace the camera database freely. Crate's
own database files are provided under the same Apache 2.0 licence as
Crate. Note that this licence covers Crate's compilation and formatting
of the data; if you intend to reuse the underlying camera data in another
project, please contact VFXCamDB and Matchmove Machine directly rather
than assuming the permission granted to Crate extends to you.

